Silverlight Community License — Proposed Custom Terms v0.1
Published October 30, 2026

These are the community terms offered by the publishing maintainer
(cosmerearchives-creator) for rights they can license in Silverlight. They are
a proposed, unreviewed custom license, not an OSI-approved open source license
and not a PolyForm license. Publication offers the permissions below now;
"proposed" describes the need for legal review, not a requirement to register
or await individual approval for a permitted use.

1. Scope and grant
"Software" means the original Silverlight code and accompanying project
documentation made available with these terms, including modifications of
that material. It excludes separately licensed third-party material and user
output. Subject to these terms, the applicable rights holders grant you a
worldwide, royalty-free, nonexclusive permission to copy, run, study, and
modify the Software for the permitted uses below, and to redistribute it only
as allowed in section 4. No rights beyond those the licensor holds are granted.

2. Permitted users and uses
(a) Anyone may use and modify the Software for personal, educational, research,
or other noncommercial purposes. This does not cover organizational commercial
deployment described in section 5.
(b) An independent individual creator may use and modify it to create and
monetize their own output without any revenue, audience, or success ceiling.
An entity wholly owned and controlled by that individual, employing no other
people in the creative undertaking, may exercise the same permission. Acting
as an employee, agent, or deployment intermediary for an otherwise ineligible
organization does not qualify as independent individual use.
(c) A qualifying small creator team may use and modify it in its own creative
work, including monetized output. At first actual use, the undertaking must
have no more than five natural persons working in it (owners, employees, and
regular contractors combined, across related entities), and be majority owned
and controlled by those active individual creators. It must not be controlled
by, a subsidiary of, or an internal unit of another organization. Splitting
one undertaking into nominally separate teams does not create eligibility.
There is no revenue ceiling.
(d) A team that qualifies under (c) is grandfathered: the same continuous
creator-controlled undertaking may keep using and modifying this licensed
version as it grows beyond five people or becomes successful. Incorporation
or a name change alone does not end this permission. Acquisition, merger
into another undertaking, or loss of majority ownership or control by its
qualifying original creators ends grandfathering for organizational commercial
use. It cannot be transferred to an acquirer, parent, affiliates, or unrelated
business. Individual creators retain their independent permission under (b).
(e) Keep reasonable private, dated records of initial qualification if relying
on (d). No submission, registration, telemetry, account, or online license
verification is required. Good-faith local records suffice absent contrary
evidence. These permissions do not require a donation, shout-out, or credit
in creative output.

3. Your output and offline use
The licensor claims no ownership of your notes, maps, research, scripts,
videos, books, or other output merely because you used Silverlight. You retain
whatever rights you otherwise have in that output and may sell or license it.
Output does not include Software copied into or distributed as a product.
You remain responsible for rights in imported material and third-party content.
The full local, offline-first core may be used without an account, sync, AI,
telemetry, or online license verification. Optional services have their own
terms and possible costs; this license promises neither their availability
nor any particular feature, future update, hosting, or support.

4. Noncommercial redistribution and modifications
You may share original or modified source and binaries free of charge for
noncommercial purposes, retaining this license, existing copyright notices,
and required third-party notices. Provide corresponding modifiable source
with binaries or a working, free source link for that exact version. Clearly
mark modifications and their author; do not imply an official release or
endorsement. Recipients receive covered material under these same terms;
you may not impose restrictions that remove these permissions. Your own
separable contributions remain yours, subject to rights needed to distribute
the combined work under these terms.
You may not sell, rent, sublicense for a fee, place behind a payment gate,
include in a paid bundle, or commercially host/provide the Software or a
modified/rebranded derivative as a product or service without a separate
written commercial license. Voluntary donations must not condition access,
features, updates, or permission to use it. Selling creative output under
sections 2–3 is expressly permitted and is not resale of the Software.

5. Separate commercial licensing
Commercial adoption by any organization outside section 2, including large
media companies, requires a separately negotiated written paid commercial
license before deployment. Software resale, commercial hosting, and selling
or commercially supplying a rebranded/custom fork also require that license,
even for an otherwise qualifying creator or team. A commercial agreement may
authorize branding or a custom fork only to the extent expressly agreed.
Start an inquiry at https://github.com/cosmerearchives-creator/Mind-Map/issues
and request a private contact route before sharing confidential details.
Issues are public and require GitHub sign-in; no fee, response time, approval,
private channel, or commercial license availability is promised by this text.

6. Third-party rights, contributions, and identity
Third-party components, fonts, artwork, and other separately licensed material
keep their own licenses; preserve and comply with those terms. These terms
do not relicense them or resolve conflicting obligations. Where a contributor
or other rights holder has not authorized this grant, obtain their permission
or omit their material. This publication does not establish a completed
dependency, provenance, or contributor-rights audit or retroactively relicense
earlier releases that did not include it.
Contributors keep their copyrights. No copyright assignment, blanket consent
to future relicensing, or right to sell others' contributions is implied.
Commercial licensing must separately clear any rights not held by the maintainer.
No trademark rights or endorsement are granted. Descriptive attribution is
allowed, but names/logos and modified branding need independent clearance;
no claim of trademark registration, exclusivity, or clearance is made.

7. Duration and breach
Permissions for a copy received under these terms continue while you comply;
a later license change does not withdraw them for that copy. Future releases
may have different terms. Permissions terminate upon material breach and
automatically reinstate if cured within 30 days after you first learn of it,
unless the breach is repeated after prior reinstatement. Termination does not
transfer ownership of your output. Rights and exceptions under applicable law
are not restricted. If a provision is unenforceable, the rest remains effective
to the extent permitted by law; no excluded use is thereby affirmatively licensed.

8. Disclaimer and limitation
TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS"
AND "AS AVAILABLE", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED,
INCLUDING MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, TITLE, AND
NONINFRINGEMENT. NO LICENSOR OR CONTRIBUTOR IS LIABLE FOR CLAIMS, DAMAGES,
OR OTHER LIABILITY ARISING FROM THE SOFTWARE OR ITS USE, WHETHER IN CONTRACT,
TORT, OR OTHERWISE, INCLUDING LOST DATA, LOST PROFITS, OR BUSINESS INTERRUPTION.
NOTHING EXCLUDES LIABILITY OR MANDATORY RIGHTS THAT CANNOT LAWFULLY BE EXCLUDED.
